{"objective":"MVP scope for the eka-mcp production-readiness requirement: contract relocation (plugin contract to eka-core), plugin command registration with trust boundary, MCP hardening + conformance, capability expansion (context + authoring tools + resources), configure UX, and versioning/pack stabilization — delivered in one execution container after plugin-install-trust and cli-experience.","scope":"Six work items in one execution container: 1. sto:mcp-contract-relocation — plugin contract types + registry move from eka-cli/plugin to eka-core/plugin (A2); eka-cli keeps runner/Discover; eka-mcp drops eka-cli dependency and removes the local pack.Manifest workaround; ADR-030 authored (supersedes ADR-023, notes the eka install removal commit 6600f38); req:prd + ADR-028 amended (consumer import rule, contract location). 2. sto:mcp-command-registration — B1 deferred registration via manifest with versioned dispatch protocol extension; trust boundary G1-G4 (official-registry-only, hash at dispatch anti-TOCTOU, plugin dir over PATH, collision refusal, manifest cache TTL) + failure semantics (≤2s probe, fail-open skip, per-process memoize); ADR-031 authored; plan:cli-experience amended for dynamic grouping (GroupID). 3. sto:mcp-hardening-conformance — batch array rejection, error message policy (refusal classes, no internal leakage), 64 MiB read line cap, fuzz 10k+ (0 crash/hang), protocol conformance suite (initialize strict 2024-11-05, ping, tools, resources, notifications, error codes), integration test with opencode. 4. sto:mcp-capability-expansion — tools context/get/domain/status + validate/new/publish/transition/note/view/draft_list/integrity_check/discard (all writes via Authoring API, explicit agent author identity); resources eka://status, eka://skills/\u003cname\u003e, eka://templates/\u003ctype\u003e (read-only from embedded pack). 5. sto:mcp-configure-ux — eka-mcp configure subcommand (opencode/claude/codex, --dir, --dry-run, --json, unsupported-target refusal) + README manual snippets + graceful no-workspace start. 6. sto:mcp-versioning-pack — bump to 1.0.0, pack status experimental to stable, requiresEka refreshed, four stale pack documents corrected.","outOfScope":"MCP advanced features (logging, prompts, sampling, roots, pagination, resource templates/subscriptions, progress); protocol versions beyond 2024-11-05; HTTP/SSE transport; multi-session concurrency; eka-discuss/eka-execute as MCP tools; sync/relate/project/export-import/feedback/update as MCP tools; eka edit as tool; sandboxing/binary signing; contract B3 rich command descriptions; FEEDBACK_ISSUE_TOKEN hardening."}